1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,812
Welcome to the updated Orders Shop, the web
front end for the Orders API.

2
00:00:04,812 --> 00:00:06,806
It is now built with Material UI,

3
00:00:06,806 --> 00:00:11,640
with clear alerts for problems and short toast
messages when something succeeds.

4
00:00:11,640 --> 00:00:14,904
It still asks you to confirm
before it saves anything.

5
00:00:14,904 --> 00:00:18,530
This tour uses the real app, running
locally with demo data.

6
00:00:18,530 --> 00:00:22,216
We start as a customer, and then
switch to the administrator.

7
00:00:24,027 --> 00:00:25,576
This is the sign-in page.

8
00:00:25,576 --> 00:00:28,179
A new customer starts with Create account.

9
00:00:28,886 --> 00:00:32,701
Registration asks for a name, an
email, and a password,

10
00:00:32,701 --> 00:00:34,782
with a label above each field.

11
00:00:34,782 --> 00:00:40,538
The form checks as you type, so a password that
is too short is flagged right away,

12
00:00:40,538 --> 00:00:42,758
in red, before anything is sent.

13
00:00:43,458 --> 00:00:47,941
The password needs at least fifteen
characters, with no composition rules,

14
00:00:47,941 --> 00:00:49,334
and spaces are allowed.

15
00:00:49,334 --> 00:00:51,212
So a short sentence works well.

16
00:00:51,212 --> 00:00:54,968
Then a confirmation dialog asks
whether to create the account,

17
00:00:54,968 --> 00:00:57,210
and nothing is sent until we say yes.

18
00:00:57,921 --> 00:01:01,089
The result is always the same
check your email message,

19
00:01:01,089 --> 00:01:03,969
whether or not the address was
already registered.

20
00:01:03,969 --> 00:01:05,985
That keeps account lookups private.

21
00:01:06,687 --> 00:01:10,587
If you try to sign in before
confirming, an alert explains why,

22
00:01:10,587 --> 00:01:13,311
and offers to resend the
confirmation email.

23
00:01:14,012 --> 00:01:16,450
In this local setup, email is simulated,

24
00:01:16,450 --> 00:01:19,802
and the confirmation link is
written to the server log.

25
00:01:19,802 --> 00:01:21,753
Opening it confirms the address,

26
00:01:21,753 --> 00:01:25,532
and the app removes the token from the
address bar right away.

27
00:01:26,233 --> 00:01:28,057
Now the customer can sign in.

28
00:01:31,792 --> 00:01:35,807
Signed-in customers land on the
catalog: eight demo products,

29
00:01:35,807 --> 00:01:38,176
each with a price and a stock state.

30
00:01:38,891 --> 00:01:42,754
Search matches name or SKU, and
starts after two characters.

31
00:01:42,754 --> 00:01:44,621
One letter only shows a hint.

32
00:01:44,621 --> 00:01:48,935
Typing key narrows the list, and the
search is kept in the address,

33
00:01:48,935 --> 00:01:50,867
so the page can be bookmarked.

34
00:01:51,578 --> 00:01:53,362
Sorting and filters work too.

35
00:01:53,362 --> 00:01:56,315
Here the list runs from most to
least expensive,

36
00:01:56,315 --> 00:02:00,314
limited to products under one hundred
dollars, and in stock only.

37
00:02:01,018 --> 00:02:03,784
Opening a product shows its
details and stock,

38
00:02:03,784 --> 00:02:06,730
with a quantity picker and an
add to cart button.

39
00:02:07,444 --> 00:02:10,674
Let's add the keyboard with the
green Add to cart button,

40
00:02:10,674 --> 00:02:12,941
and then a wireless mouse from the list.

41
00:02:12,941 --> 00:02:15,604
The cart count in the header
updates each time.

42
00:02:16,315 --> 00:02:19,984
In the cart, quantities can be
changed and products removed,

43
00:02:19,984 --> 00:02:21,940
and the estimated total follows.

44
00:02:21,940 --> 00:02:25,915
The cart lives in this browser, and is
cleared when you sign out.

45
00:02:26,627 --> 00:02:30,407
Placing the order asks for
confirmation in a Material dialog,

46
00:02:30,407 --> 00:02:34,187
then checks current prices and stock,
and sends it just once.

47
00:02:34,187 --> 00:02:36,790
The new order opens right away as pending,

48
00:02:36,790 --> 00:02:39,640
and a toast message says the
order was placed.

49
00:02:39,640 --> 00:02:42,491
It shows the items, total, and
status history.

50
00:02:43,195 --> 00:02:48,085
My orders lists every order, with filters for
status and dates, and sorting.

51
00:02:48,085 --> 00:02:50,659
The filters stay in the address as well.

52
00:02:51,372 --> 00:02:54,817
A pending order can be cancelled,
with an optional reason.

53
00:02:54,817 --> 00:02:59,628
A toast confirms it, the status changes to
cancelled, and the history records it.

54
00:03:00,342 --> 00:03:02,203
My account shows the profile.

55
00:03:02,203 --> 00:03:03,678
The email is read only.

56
00:03:03,678 --> 00:03:06,951
Edit profile changes the name
and the phone number.

57
00:03:06,951 --> 00:03:10,608
Save changes stays disabled until
something is different,

58
00:03:10,608 --> 00:03:12,725
and saving asks for confirmation.

59
00:03:12,725 --> 00:03:16,254
When it is saved, a toast says the
profile was updated.

60
00:03:16,967 --> 00:03:19,824
Changing the password asks for
confirmation too.

61
00:03:19,824 --> 00:03:24,407
It then signs you out on every device, so you
sign in again with the new one.

62
00:03:30,643 --> 00:03:34,579
Sign out everywhere ends the sessions
on all devices at once.

63
00:03:35,292 --> 00:03:38,705
If you forget the password, enter
the email, confirm,

64
00:03:38,705 --> 00:03:41,023
and you always see the same message.

65
00:03:41,023 --> 00:03:46,240
The reset link, again from the server log,
opens a page to choose a new password.

66
00:03:46,240 --> 00:03:49,524
After one more confirmation, you
return to sign-in.

67
00:03:52,728 --> 00:03:55,064
Customers cannot open the back office.

68
00:03:55,064 --> 00:03:58,200
The admin address shows a
not-allowed page instead.

69
00:03:58,910 --> 00:04:01,137
Delete account explains what happens.

70
00:04:01,137 --> 00:04:05,050
Personal details are erased, order
records are kept without them,

71
00:04:05,050 --> 00:04:06,796
and you cannot sign in again.

72
00:04:06,796 --> 00:04:09,926
It asks for the current password
and a confirmation.

73
00:04:10,628 --> 00:04:13,868
Afterwards, the same
credentials no longer work.

74
00:04:17,729 --> 00:04:22,030
Administrators sign in on the same page,
and land in the back office.

75
00:04:22,030 --> 00:04:26,705
The dashboard shows the low-stock count, and
the last thirty days of sales.

76
00:04:27,413 --> 00:04:32,491
The Products section lists every product,
with search, sorting, and paging.

77
00:04:32,491 --> 00:04:37,637
The Edit button is orange and Delete is red,
so the risky action stands out.

78
00:04:38,342 --> 00:04:41,295
Creating a product validates
the form first.

79
00:04:41,295 --> 00:04:46,798
Then the name, SKU, description, price, and
stock are saved, after a confirmation,

80
00:04:46,798 --> 00:04:49,550
and a toast says the product was created.

81
00:04:50,313 --> 00:04:54,473
Editing loads the latest version and
saves with a concurrency check,

82
00:04:54,473 --> 00:04:57,593
so two admins cannot silently
overwrite each other.

83
00:04:57,593 --> 00:05:00,897
Here I raise the stock, and a
toast confirms the save.

84
00:05:01,597 --> 00:05:03,510
Deleting asks for confirmation.

85
00:05:03,510 --> 00:05:06,904
It is a soft delete: customers
stop seeing the product,

86
00:05:06,904 --> 00:05:09,188
and existing orders keep their lines.

87
00:05:09,188 --> 00:05:11,533
A toast says the product was archived.

88
00:05:12,244 --> 00:05:15,818
With Include deleted ticked, the
product shows as deleted,

89
00:05:15,818 --> 00:05:18,652
and one click restores it,
with another toast.

90
00:05:20,616 --> 00:05:24,762
That is the customer portal, and the
first part of the back office.

91
00:05:24,762 --> 00:05:27,609
Screens for customers, orders,
reports, users,

92
00:05:27,609 --> 00:05:30,332
and audit logs are not in the
interface yet.

93
00:05:30,332 --> 00:05:33,054
For now those are available
through the API.

94
00:05:33,054 --> 00:05:37,943
To try it yourself, start the stack with
docker compose up, and open localhost,

95
00:05:37,943 --> 00:05:39,552
port eight zero eight one.
